{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 27,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Boast not thyself of to-morrow;\nFor thou knowest not what a day may bring forth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth;\nA stranger, and not thine own lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A stone is heavy, and the sand weighty;\nBut a fool’s vexation is heavier than they both.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wrath is cruel, and anger is overwhelming;\nBut who is able to stand before jealousy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better is open rebuke\nThan love that is hidden.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Faithful are the wounds of a friend;\nBut the kisses of an enemy are profuse.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The full soul loatheth a honeycomb;\nBut to the hungry soul every bitter thing is sweet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a bird that wandereth from her nest,\nSo is a man that wandereth from his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oil and perfume rejoice the heart;\nSo doth the sweetness of a man’s friend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of hearty counsel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thine own friend, and thy father’s friend, forsake not;\nAnd go not to thy brother’s house in the day of thy calamity:\nBetter is a neighbor that is near than a brother far off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, be wise, and make my heart glad,\nThat I may answer him that reproacheth me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A prudent man seeth the evil, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hideth himself;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "But",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the simple pass on, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " suffer for it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take his garment that is surety for a stranger;\nAnd hold him in pledge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is surety",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a foreign woman.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that blesseth his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning,\nIt shall be counted a curse to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A continual dropping in a very rainy day\nAnd a contentious woman are alike:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that would restrain her restraineth the wind;\nAnd his right hand encountereth oil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Iron sharpeneth iron;\nSo a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso keepeth the fig-tree shall eat the fruit thereof;\nAnd he that regardeth his master shall be honored.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As in water face ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "answereth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to face,\nSo the heart of man to man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied;\nAnd the eyes of man are never satisfied.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The refining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold;\nAnd a man is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "tried",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by his praise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though thou shouldest bray a fool in a mortar with a pestle along with bruised grain,\nYet will not his foolishness depart from him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " look well to thy herds:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For riches are not for ever;\nAnd doth the crown endure unto all generations?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The hay is carried, and the tender grass showeth itself,\nAnd the herbs of the mountains are gathered in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lambs are for thy clothing,\nAnd the goats are the price of the field;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.27.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.27.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " goats’ milk enough for thy food, for the food of thy household,\nAnd maintenance for thy maidens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
